                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers[/h1]\n\nI don't know why this game has Positive review status on Steam. Were the other VR games out back on December 15, 2016 even worse than this? That's hard to imagine. I paid $1.49 USD for this on a Steam sale and now I wish I had just burned my money instead of trying to burn those skellies & Santa (Santa Skelly) to hell.\n\nThis is a 360 stand still wave shooter where you spam throw fireballs instead of shooting a gun. While initially fun, that fun quickly dissipates after about 10 minutes .... if you're the patient-type like me. It'll get boring after 5 minutes for normal people. \n\nYou have an undead army just walking straight to you. They are either melee or ranged (shooting this green gaseous ball at you). Each wave just brings more of them. You can in theory use a shield or an arcane fire spell. I said in theory, because of course, it's just better to spam the fireballs with each hand. \n\n[b]Rate 4/10. But you don't need to take my word for it, you can watch the video proof below.[/b]\n\nhttps://youtu.be/gaQAk-ldZdM",
